{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1513"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge music-stage/theatre","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/music-stage__theatre.json","changes":[{"field":"titleEn","old":"Swans and Fauns: Five Dancers Who Defined Twentieth-Century Ballet","new":"Swans and Fauns: Six Dancers Who Defined Twentieth-Century Ballet"},{"field":"titleDe","old":"Schwäne und Faune: Fünf Tänzer, die das Ballett des 20. Jahrhunderts prägten","new":"Schwäne und Faune: Sechs Tänzer, die das Ballett des 20. Jahrhunderts prägten"},{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",54],["-","Five"],["+","Six"],["=",753],["+","The last of the great defectors was Mikhail Baryshnikov, born in Riga in 1948 and trained in Leningrad, where he became a star of the Kirov. On 29 June 1974, during a tour of Canada, he slipped away from his Soviet minders in Toronto and asked for political asylum. In the West he joined American Ballet Theatre, spent some fifteen months with George Balanchine's New York City Ballet and directed ABT from 1980 to 1989. He also became an actor: \"The Turning Point\" (1977) earned him an Oscar nomination, and in the sixth and final season of \"Sex and the City\" he played the Russian artist Aleksandr Petrovsky, Carrie Bradshaw's lover.\n\n"],["=",127],["+","\n| Mikhail Baryshnikov | 1948, Riga | Kirov, American Ballet Theatre |"]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",56],["-","Fünf"],["+","Sechs"],["=",761],["+","Der letzte der großen Überläufer war Mikhail Baryshnikov (auch Michail Baryschnikow), 1948 in Riga geboren und in Leningrad ausgebildet, wo er zum Star des Kirow-Balletts wurde. Am 29. Juni 1974 setzte er sich während einer Kanada-Tournee in Toronto von seinen sowjetischen Aufpassern ab und bat um politisches Asyl. Im Westen tanzte er beim American Ballet Theatre, verbrachte etwa fünfzehn Monate bei George Balanchines New York City Ballet und leitete das ABT von 1980 bis 1989. Er wurde auch Schauspieler: „Am Wendepunkt“ (1977) brachte ihm eine Oscar-Nominierung ein, und in der sechsten und letzten Staffel von „Sex and the City“ spielte er den russischen Künstler Aleksandr Petrovsky, den Geliebten von Carrie Bradshaw.\n\n"],["=",125],["+","\n| Mikhail Baryshnikov | 1948, Riga | Kirow, American Ballet Theatre |"]]}]},
